get.description:
Every flagged or marked name across the active basket union at ``asof``, each with the theses holding
it — the Admin list and the Board's marks (a marker never marks a ticker). Computed on read, never stored;
display-only.

AdminPriceRepairsOut.description:
The "Price feed repairs" panel (T2 + Q8 + T3 + T7): one place for every feed decision the operator
owes or has made. The INVENTORY (``renamed`` / ``unpriceable`` / ``closed``) comes from the newest
finished, full-roster live run artifact that evaluated recency (``asof`` / ``ran_at``); the DECISIONS are
read LIVE from the append-only repair logs, so a click shows at once: an acknowledged name moves from
``unpriceable`` to ``acknowledged``, an Adopt shows as the row's ``change`` with its Undo. Read-only.

- ``renamed`` — loud: the splice-probed successors, each with Adopt (and Undo once adopted);
- ``unpriceable`` — loud: never priced, not acknowledged — Set symbol / Acknowledge / Remove;
- ``acknowledged`` — QUIET: every active acknowledgment, each revocable;
- ``closed`` — QUIET: names that stopped trading (T1) — no repair; their vendor 404 is expected (T3);
- ``applied`` — every STANDING operator price-symbol change, each with its Undo (the inverse stays
  visible after the repair healed the tape and the name left the inventory, WB#1);
- ``expected_misses`` — how many vendor 404s that pass excused as expected (closed / acknowledged);
- ``successor`` (T7) — loud: members whose company now files under a NEW CIK (the filing legs read the
  dead one), each with its recommended successor to Adopt (and Undo once adopted). From the newest
  finished, full-roster live artifact whose successor scan RAN (``successor_asof``);
- ``cik_applied`` (T7) — every STANDING successor-CIK re-point, each with its Undo (WB#1);
- ``limitations`` (0056) — QUIET: the known feed limitations ("the vendor serves no history"), the
  newest mark per name — active ones with their Undo, then undone ones (grayed, "Mark again").
``probe_error`` = the rename probe failed on that pass (``renamed`` rows then carry no verdict);
``successor_error`` = the newest live pass's successor scan failed (its rows then are the last good
pass's, or none).

AdminSplitListSecOut.description:
The SEC filing behind a split: the extractor's reading and the LOCATED passage, verbatim.
``date_kind`` = ``trading`` (the filing states the first session) or ``legal`` (a legal effective date);
``abstain_reason`` = why no single ratio was read.

BackupCreateIn.description:
The optional create body. A ``label`` marks a NAMED snapshot (a deliberate recovery point like
``pre-migration``), which retention keeps 90 days, or while it is among the newest 20 labeled dumps;
omit it for a rolling nightly-style dump.

CrossNearNameOut.description:
A name whose 50d sits within ``near_band_pct``% of its 200d, the gap smaller than ``near_lookback``
sessions before, with no cross within ``recent_sessions``. ``gap_pct`` = (SMA50 / SMA200 − 1) %;
``change`` = ``gap_pct − gap_pct_then``, in points. The tape only, never a forecast.

OnboardingNameOut.description:
X1 — one name in the staged onboarding queue (``security_onboarding``). ``legs_done`` is its checkpoint;
``in_live_basket`` false = PARKED (no live basket holds it any more, so the job leaves it — re-adding the
name resumes it). ``last_error`` is the latest leg failure (on a ``done`` row: a tail leg's note).

SharedNameChipOut.description:
One card a company sits on. ``links`` = its links there (basket order; ``null`` = no link);
``silent_link`` = "Context" / "Bench" when that is its membership there; ``counts`` = it has a
non-silent row on that card. ``ticker`` = its ticker on that card (the Cockpit's ``?name=`` key).
